<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Choose the inverse of each transformation.</p><div>(a) the reflection in the y-axis: [ it has no inverse | reflection in the x-axis | reflection in the y-axis | reflection in the line y = x | reflection in the line y = −x | rotation of 90° anticlockwise about O | rotation of 180° about O | rotation of 90° clockwise about O | enlargement, centre O, scale factor 1/3 | enlargement, centre O, scale factor −(1/3) | enlargement, centre O, scale factor 3 | enlargement, centre O, scale factor −3 ]  </div><div>(b) the reflection in the x-axis: [ it has no inverse | reflection in the x-axis | reflection in the y-axis | reflection in the line y = x | reflection in the line y = −x | rotation of 90° anticlockwise about O | rotation of 180° about O | rotation of 90° clockwise about O | enlargement, centre O, scale factor 1/3 | enlargement, centre O, scale factor −(1/3) | enlargement, centre O, scale factor 3 | enlargement, centre O, scale factor −3 ]  </div><div>(c) the enlargement, centre O, scale factor <m>{\frac{1}{3}}</m>: [ it has no inverse | reflection in the x-axis | reflection in the y-axis | reflection in the line y = x | reflection in the line y = −x | rotation of 90° anticlockwise about O | rotation of 180° about O | rotation of 90° clockwise about O | enlargement, centre O, scale factor 1/3 | enlargement, centre O, scale factor −(1/3) | enlargement, centre O, scale factor 3 | enlargement, centre O, scale factor −3 ]  </div><div>(d) the rotation of <m>90^\circ</m> clockwise about O: [ it has no inverse | reflection in the x-axis | reflection in the y-axis | reflection in the line y = x | reflection in the line y = −x | rotation of 90° anticlockwise about O | rotation of 180° about O | rotation of 90° clockwise about O | enlargement, centre O, scale factor 1/3 | enlargement, centre O, scale factor −(1/3) | enlargement, centre O, scale factor 3 | enlargement, centre O, scale factor −3 ]  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The inverse undoes the transformation, so it sends every image point back to where it came from.</p><ul><li>(a) The inverse of the reflection in the y-axis is the reflection in the y-axis itself.</li><li>(b) The inverse of the reflection in the x-axis is the reflection in the x-axis itself.</li><li>(c) The inverse of the enlargement, centre O, scale factor <m>{\frac{1}{3}}</m> is the enlargement, centre O, scale factor <m>{3}</m>.</li><li>(d) The inverse of the rotation of <m>90^\circ</m> clockwise about O is the rotation of <m>90^\circ</m> anticlockwise about O.</li></ul><p>A reflection is its own inverse; a quarter turn is undone by a quarter turn the other way; a half turn is its own inverse; an enlargement with scale factor k is undone by scale factor <m>\frac{1}{k}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>reflection in the y-axis</p></answer>
    <answer><p>reflection in the x-axis</p></answer>
    <answer><p>enlargement, centre O, scale factor 3</p></answer>
    <answer><p>rotation of 90° anticlockwise about O</p></answer>
</stack-static>